body:
## Describe the problem/error/question

When using the Zoho CRM node ("Create a lead" operation, resource: lead) to create a lead whose email **address already** exists in Zoho, the node throws a generic/unknown error instead of returning a clear, informative message about the duplicate record. I would expect n8n to surface Zoho's actual API error (e.g. "duplicate data" / record already exists) rather than a generic "unknown issue" error.

## What is the error message (if any)?

```json
{
  "errorMessage": "There was an unknown issue while executing the node",
  "errorDescription": "Double-check the node configuration and the service it connects to. Check the error details below and refer to the n8n documentation to troubleshoot the issue.",
  "errorDetails": {},
  "n8nDetails": {
    "nodeName": "Create a lead",
    "nodeType": "n8n-nodes-base.zohoCrm",
    "nodeVersion": 1,
    "resource": "lead",
    "operation": "create",
    "time": "7/24/2026, 3:28:05 PM",
    "n8nVersion": "2.31.5 (Self Hosted)",
    "binaryDataMode": "filesystem",
    "stackTrace": [
      "NodeApiError: There was an unknown issue while executing the node",
      "    at ExecuteContext.zohoApiRequest (.../n8n-nodes-base/nodes/Zoho/GenericFunctions.ts:82:9)",
      "    at processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:104:5)",
      "    at ExecuteContext.execute (.../n8n-nodes-base/nodes/Zoho/ZohoCrm.node.ts:751:22)",
      "    at WorkflowExecute.executeNode (.../n8n-core/src/execution-engine/workflow-execute.ts:1081:8)",
      "    at WorkflowExecute.runNode (.../n8n-core/src/execution-engine/workflow-execute.ts:1381:11)"
    ]
  }
}
```

