### Bug Description

Code node autocomplete stops working for named-node references when the referenced node’s execution data contains a JSON property whose name is not a valid unquoted TypeScript identifier.

(Referenced this below as well, but i recorded a [loom](https://www.loom.com/share/6350c4b587d14e478833b0b4b933ab03) with the example-workflow in the "to reproduce" section).

Examples of triggering property names include:
```ts
testing Stuff
content-type
x-request-id
```
After executing the referenced node, typing the following in a downstream Code node produces no autocomplete suggestions:

```ts const data = $('Source Node').```

The workflow still executes correctly. This appears to affect only editor autocomplete/type inference.

