### Expected behavior

Autocomplete works as expected in a code node even when a key is valid javascript like so: 

`{ "name works": 10 }` or `{ "name-works": 10 }`.

### Debug Info

I don't have any specific debug info myself. I did run a (lengthy) session with GPT SOL and it had some thoughts after about 30 minutes. 

I wasn't sure whether to include this, apologies if it's not useful. Feel free to ignore it, but it does SEEM correct so far.

<5.6-sol-bug-explanation>
The apparent cause is the dynamic TypeScript declaration generator:
[packages/frontend/editor-ui/src/features/shared/editors/plugins/codemirror/typescript/worker/dynamicTypes.ts](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/blob/n8n%402.29.8/packages/frontend/editor-ui/src/features/shared/editors/plugins/codemirror/typescript/worker/dynamicTypes.ts#L34-L39)

It currently inserts schema keys without quoting or escaping them:

```ts
const key = prop.key ?? 'unknown';
const type = processSchema(prop);
return `  ${key}: ${type};`;
```

For this JSON:

```ts
{
  "testing Stuff": 10
}
```

the generated declaration is effectively:

```ts
interface SourceNodeJson {
  testing Stuff: number;
}
```

This is invalid TypeScript. Once the generated declaration fails to parse, the TypeScript language service can no longer provide the return type or completions for $('Source Node').

The generated property name should be emitted as a valid quoted TypeScript property, for example:

```ts
interface SourceNodeJson {
  "testing Stuff": number;
}
```

The faulty generator was introduced with the TypeScript-backed Code editor in n8n 1.74.0 via [PR #12285](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/12285). The relevant code remains unchanged in 2.32.0 beta and current master.

</5.6-sol-bug-explanation>

